Mesa (KosmicKrisp): unroll loops before local arrays are lowered

What: kk_nir_options gets max_unroll_iterations = 32 (as Asahi's compiler for
the same GPUs), and msl_preprocess_nir unrolls loops with a known trip count
(nir_opt_loop_unroll in a small optimisation loop) before function-temp arrays
are lowered to scratch memory or to if-else trees.
Why: KosmicKrisp never unrolled a loop (max_unroll_iterations was 0, so
nir_opt_loop_unroll did nothing), and it lowers local arrays early. A loop
whose trip count comes from specialization constants, such as llama.cpp's
Vulkan matmul (mul_mm.comp: 2 x 2 inner loops over cache_a/cache_b and the
sums array), then indexed its arrays with a loop counter: the sums went to
'uchar scratch[128]' (thread memory, 1-byte aligned) and the caches became
if-else trees of selects, in the hottest loop. Unrolled first, the indices
are constants and the arrays become registers (no scratch left in the
kernel's MSL, MESA_KK_DEBUG=msl).
Numbers, natively on the Mac, base vs this patch alternating, nothing else
running. Mac mini M4 (macOS 27.0): llama.cpp b11760 Vulkan, Llama 3.2 3B
Q4_K_M, prompt pp512 / generation tg128 t/s 160 -> 196 / 45 -> 45 (MoltenVK
403 / 42, Metal 550 / 46); Dawn's WebGPU matmul (the harness of
mesa-kosmickrisp-shared-align.patch, robust access) 1162 -> 1162 GFLOPS.
MacBook Air M2 (macOS 27.0.1): llama.cpp Llama 3.2 1B Q4_K_M (-ub 128) pp512
141 -> 327, tg128 62.3 -> 63.4 t/s; Dawn's WebGPU matmul 758 -> 545-577 GFLOPS
(-24 to -28 %, likely register pressure). MacBook Pro M1 Max (macOS 27.0.1):
llama.cpp 3B pp512 137.5 / 137.6 -> 316.6 / 316.2, tg128 ~56 -> ~57 t/s; Dawn's
WebGPU matmul 2043-2045 -> 2045-2046 GFLOPS (no change). In a VM on the M4
(4 CPU / 6 GB, Venus): llama.cpp pp512 159 -> 194 t/s, whisper.cpp v1.9.5
base.en encoder 104 -> 76 ms (two separate VM sessions).
Trade-off: WebGPU matmul on the M2 (WebGPU in the VM is the opt-in launcher).
Upstream: not sent yet.
Tests: Vulkan CTS 1.4.7.0 on KosmicKrisp before and after, natively on a
MacBook Air M2 (macOS 27.0.1), the lists of mesa-kosmickrisp-shared-align.patch
(compute pipelines, memory model, SPIR-V compute, GLSL loops/arrays/indexing,
graphicsfuzz, samples of subgroups and tessellation/geometry): 50,788 cases
listed, 18,176 of them ran (the rest NotSupported), the same result for every
case (18,175 Pass, 1 Fail that fails before too). llama.cpp and the matmul
harness as above.
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
@@ -2272,6 +2272,28 @@
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_var_copies);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_split_var_copies);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_memcpy);
+
+   /* Unroll loops with a known trip count before the arrays they index are
+    * lowered to scratch or to if-else trees below: once unrolled, the indices
+    * are constants and nir_split_array_vars turns small per-thread arrays
+    * (a matmul's accumulators and caches) into registers.
+    */
+   bool unrolled;
+   do {
+      unrolled = false;
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_lower_vars_to_ssa);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_copy_prop);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_dce);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_dead_cf);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_cse);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_deref);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_constant_folding);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_algebraic);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_if, 0);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_remove_phis);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_loop);
+      NIR_PASS(unrolled, nir, nir_opt_loop_unroll);
+   } while (unrolled);
 
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_split_array_vars,
             nir_var_function_temp | nir_var_shader_in | nir_var_shader_out);
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.h
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.h
@@ -129,6 +129,7 @@
    .lower_uadd_carry = true,
    .lower_usub_borrow = true,
    .compact_arrays = true,
+   .max_unroll_iterations = 32,
    /* Metal does not support double. */
    .lower_doubles_options = (nir_lower_doubles_options)(~0),
    .lower_int64_options = nir_lower_ufind_msb64 | nir_lower_subgroup_shuffle64,
